        "title": "Suppress websocket send errors",
        "summary": "Comment out console.error in APIRealtimeClient send action catch block. Relies on automatic reconnection for error recovery. Affects common/src/websockets/websocket-client.ts.",
        "significance": "minor",
        "at": "2026-09-15T16:28:26.565Z"
      },
      "eli5": {
        "text": "When the app tries to send a message over the live connection and that send fails, it no longer prints a red error message to the developer console. Instead of alerting you to the glitch, the system relies on its built-in ability to reconnect automatically whenever the connection drops. If you are watching the developer tools, you will notice that failed sends are silent rather than being logged as errors.",
